  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q11",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "When $P(x)=2x^3-x^2+ax+b$ is divided by $(x-1)$ the remainder is 16, and when it is divided by $(x+2)$ the remainder is $-17$. Find $a$ and $b$ using simultaneous equations.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=4$, $b=11$. Use $a+b=15$ and $-2a+b=3$.",
      "worked": "By the remainder theorem, $P(1)=16$ and $P(-2)=-17$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(1)^3-(1)^2+a+b&=16\\\\a+b&=15\\qquad(1)\\\\2(-2)^3-(-2)^2-2a+b&=-17\\\\-2a+b&=3\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (2) from (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}3a&=12\\\\a&=4\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}4+b&=15\\\\b&=11\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
